If you build a full-screen mobile editor as a position: fixed overlay with a fixed toolbar on top and a nav bar on the bottom, iOS Safari will happily scroll your entire chrome off-screen the moment the soft keyboard opens — but only when the content is short. The fix isn't a JavaScript viewport dance. It's one line:
.editor .ProseMirror {
  padding-bottom: 60vh;
}

Give the inner scroll container something to scroll, and iOS keeps the scroll inside it instead of falling back to scrolling the document (which drags your "fixed" elements along). No html/body locking required.
I hit this while building the mobile editor for PenPage, a local-first WYSIWYG markdown notes app (React + TipTap/ProseMirror). Everything below is verified on a real iOS device.
